Exposes the legacy `codex/event/mcp_startup_update` event as an API v2 notification.

The legacy event has this shape:
```
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize, Serialize, JsonSchema, TS)]
pub struct McpStartupUpdateEvent {
    /// Server name being started.
    pub server: String,
    /// Current startup status.
    pub status: McpStartupStatus,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Deserialize, Serialize, JsonSchema, TS)]
#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case", tag = "state")]
#[ts(rename_all = "snake_case", tag = "state")]
pub enum McpStartupStatus {
    Starting,
    Ready,
    Failed { error: String },
    Cancelled,
}
```

This patch fixes:
  ```diff
  diff --git a/codex-cli/bin/codex.js b/codex-cli/bin/codex.js
  index 67ab3e2d9..3e0f8570e 100755
  --- a/codex-cli/bin/codex.js
  +++ b/codex-cli/bin/codex.js
  @@ -7,6 +7,9 @@ import { createRequire } from "node:module";
   import path from "path";
   import { fileURLToPath } from "url";

  +process.title = "codex";
  +
   // __dirname equivalent in ESM
   const __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);
   const __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);
  ```

